userStories.description:
**Goal** — Choose a base-owned frozen install using packageManager and run ordered frozen lockfile fallbacks in bot review and fix, reporting the install that succeeded.

**Motivation** — The repo uses npm (`package-lock.json`) and keeps a stale `bun.lock`.

**Approach** — **US-001 — lockfile choice and fallback.** `lockfileCommands` checks every `LOCKFILE_COMMANDS` entry with `readBaseFile` (so a read or inspection failure still throws, as today) and collects the present ones. It then reads base `package.json` and takes `packageManager`'s name before the first `@` (`"npm@10.9.0"` -> `npm`); a missing or unparseable `package.json`, or a non-string `packageManager`, is ignored. If a present entry has that `manager` and an `install`, it is chosen with reason `package-manager`; otherwise the first present entry, reason `lockfile-order`. `fallbacks` are the other present entries that have an `install`, each as `{ command, timeoutSeconds: DERIVED_INSTALL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS }`, minus any whose command equals the chosen one. The detected tier's gate prefix follows the chosen entry. `BotChecks.install` is set where the derived install becomes `preRun` (the detected tier, and the install fallback in `resolveBotChecks`); never for a configured `execution.preRun` or an install extracted from AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md. `runBotInstall` calls `run({ steps: checks.preRun, workdir })`; when that throws `PRE_RUN_FAILED` and `checks.install?.fallbacks` is non-empty, it logs a `[WARN]` naming the failed command and the next one, then calls `run` with each fallback as a single-step list until one succeeds. When every attempt fails it throws `PRE_RUN_FAILED` with `context.command` = the first failed command and `context.tried` = every command attempted, in order. Any other error propagates at once. Every lockfile entry is now inspected (today the loop stops at the first present one), so an inspection failure on a later lockfile also fails the derivation; a `package.json` inspection or read failure (not a missing file) fails it the same way.

**Integration** — `LOCKFILE_COMMANDS` (`bot/checks.ts`). Baseline: `{ path, prefix, install }` entries. Target: each entry also carries `manager: "bun" | "npm" | "pnpm" | "yarn"`; order unchanged.
`lockfileCommands(input)` (`bot/checks.ts`). Baseline: returns the first present entry's `{ prefix, install? }`, else `{ prefix: "npm run" }`. Target: returns `LockfileChoice` (below).
`BotChecks` (`bot/checks.ts`). Baseline: `{ source, gates, preRun }`. Target: gains optional `install?: BotInstallChoice`, set only when `preRun` is the single step derived from a lockfile.
`prepareReviewChecks` (`bot/review-run.ts`) and `initialFixState` (`bot/fix-run.ts`). Baseline: call `runPreRunSteps({ steps: checks.preRun, ... })` through their deps object. Target: call `runBotInstall(checks, workdir, run)` with `run` = `_botReviewDeps.runPreRunSteps` / `_botFixDeps.runPreRunSteps`. The build steps keep calling the deps object directly.
`initialFixState(env, outputDir, input)` (`bot/fix-run.ts`). Baseline: returns `BotFixState`. Target (US-001): returns `{ state: BotFixState; checks: BotChecks }`, where `checks` is `env.checks` with `preRun` replaced by `runBotInstall`'s `ran` after a successful install (the `readyOnly` early return and a failed setup return `env.checks` unchanged); `executeFix` runs the step graph with `{ ...env, checks }`, so the fix prompt's checkout state lists the install that ran. US-002 extends the same return for the re-resolved install.
`prepareReviewChecks` setup reporting (`bot/review-run.ts`). Target (US-001): the checks it returns carry `preRun` = `runBotInstall`'s `ran` after a successful install, so the review's checkout state and summary setup list name the install that ran.

**Scope** — In: checks.ts lockfile selection/metadata, new install.ts, command-owned setup wiring, successful-step reporting and associated tests. Out: US-002 saved-install re-resolution, setupHint and persisted install validation; US-003/004 rebase scope/carry. A non-frozen install (`bun install`, `npm install`) as any fallback: it rewrites a lockfile the fix session could commit (#3026 ruling). Install fallbacks for a configured `execution.preRun` or an install extracted from instruction files. Changing the saved review artifact's checks after a fallback or re-resolved install succeeds; only the running command's checks change. Reading the package manager from AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md prose for the derived install; only `package.json` `packageManager` is read. Recording the review's own install failure in the review artifact; `nax bot fix` detects a failing saved install by running it. Changing the `--in-place` cleanliness check: a fallback or re-resolved install that dirties an in-place checkout ends `setup-failed` with "in-place checkout not clean after setup", as any install does today.

**Interface** — New types (`bot/checks.ts`):
```ts
export type InstallReason = "package-manager" | "lockfile-order";
export interface BotInstallChoice {
  /** The lockfile the install was derived from, e.g. "bun.lock". */
  readonly lockfile: string;
  readonly reason: InstallReason;
  /** Frozen installs of the other lockfiles present on the base, in LOCKFILE_COMMANDS order, deduplicated by command. */
  readonly fallbacks: readonly PreRunStepConfig[];
}
interface LockfileChoice {
  readonly prefix: string;
  readonly install?: string;
  readonly lockfile?: string;
  readonly reason?: InstallReason;
  readonly fallbacks: readonly PreRunStepConfig[];
}
```
New module `bot/install.ts` (US-001):
```ts
/** Runs checks.preRun with `run`; on PRE_RUN_FAILED with checks.install fallbacks, runs each fallback once, in order. */
export async function runBotInstall(
  checks: BotChecks,
  workdir: string,
  run: typeof runPreRunSteps,
): Promise<{ ran: readonly PreRunStepConfig[] }>;
```
Read-only contract: `PreRunStepConfig { command: string; timeoutSeconds: number }`; `runPreRunSteps({ steps, workdir }): Promise<void>` throws `NaxError` `PRE_RUN_FAILED` with `context.command` on the first failing step; `DERIVED_INSTALL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 600`. Test the wrapper with command A/B/C failures and exercise both runBotReview and runBotFix using their own runPreRunSteps seams. Update whole-result expectations for bun scripts and install-capable lockfile rows, but leave yarn/no-lockfile without install metadata. Read base package.json for packageManager only when two or more lockfiles are present; with one or no lockfile never read it, so the existing config-tier test asserting no package.json read stays unchanged.
